[review] ### Summary
[review] This PR fixes a bug in `torch/distributed/elastic/rendezvous/etcd_server.py`'s `find_free_port` where an uninitialized socket variable caused an `UnboundLocalError` during socket creation failures. The fix initializes the socket variable to `None` before the try block and conditionally closes it only if it was successfully created, allowing the function to properly iterate over addresses and raise a suitable exception on failure. A targeted regression test that simulates socket creation failure on the first attempt was added. The fix is minimal, well-tested, and addresses the issue thoroughly.
[review] 
[review] ### Walkthrough
[review] - `find_free_port` in `torch/distributed/elastic/rendezvous/etcd_server.py`:  
[review]   Initializes socket variable before the try block to avoid `UnboundLocalError` when socket creation fails.
[review] - Conditional socket close added to prevent closing an uninitialized socket.
[review] - Added regression test in `test/distributed/elastic/rendezvous/etcd_server_test.py` ensuring
